# Generated files are written byte-for-byte by their generators (ts-rs, xtask
# fixtures), always with LF. Without this, a Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true materialises them as CRLF, and the moment a gate
# regenerates them all 35 show as phantom-modified with an empty diff --
# inviting either a pointless commit or a reflex `checkout --` that one day
# discards a real regeneration.
# The shell-integration scripts are embedded byte-for-byte by include_str! and
# written into a shim the shell sources -- for bash, a shell on the other side
# of a WSL boundary. A CRLF checkout on Windows would ship the CR into a Linux
# bash, which fails every line with `$'\r': command not found`.
crates/zest-pty/shell-integration/** text eol=lf
crates/zest-proto/bindings/** text eol=lf
crates/zest-proto/fixtures/** text eol=lf
schemas/** text eol=lf
clients/web/packages/settings/generated/** text eol=lf
clients/web/packages/theme/src/builtin.generated.ts text eol=lf
